  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Hot temperatures, high humidity, and severe \nthunderstorm chances again today into Saturday.  \n\nMid/upper impulse paired with a notable low-level theta-e\nridge/moisture plume is triggering scattered to numerous\nthunderstorms over WV into western MD and VA. Expect this to\ncontinue and congeal into one or more clusters as storms press\nsoutheastward generally near and southwest of the Potomac River\nthrough early this evening. The timing is much more in the\ntypical climo window compared to yesterday's late evening event.\nDamaging wind gusts are the main threat, though some hail is\npossible especially in any semi-discrete/lead cells. Mid-level\nlapse rates have lessened a bit but shear will increase to\naround 40 kts by this evening which could compensate. Increased\nflow and moderate to high MLCAPE (1500-2500 J/kg) and DCAPE\n(900-1400 J/kg) will support a damaging wind risk.\n\nStorms should gradually wane in intensity and coverage by late\nevening, though continued height falls and the approach of a\nsurface front may continue at least spotty activity through much\nof the night.\n\nNotably cooler Sat with some showers or thunderstorms associated \nwith a disturbance aloft. There remains notable uncertainty wrt \ncoverage. Lower odds for SVR wx Sat with SPC only having the FA in \nGeneral Thunder. Some models much more bullish than others, with the \ngreatest likelihood of precip across the SW half of the FA. Highs \nSat in the 80s for most. \n\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...Drier conditions expected for the second half of \nLabor Day weekend through early next week.\n\nSfc high pressure over the GL will track over the Mid-Atlantic Sun \ninto Mon, with accompanying mid-level dry air that will bring down \nhumidity and t-storm chances. Daily highs drop to the low 80s, along \nwith drier dewpoints in the mid to upper 50s. These conditions \nlikely persist through Tue as high pressure drifts south.\n\nAs high pressure dominates, expect temps to slowly creep back up to \nthe mid-to-upper 80s beginning Tue and Wed. Entering into the \nmidweek, broad upper-level ridging begins to build over the southern \nPlains, with a deep trough forming to the north over Nova Scotia. \nThis will create a frontal boundary tracking across the East Coast \nsometime during this period, potentially beginning Wed and into Thu. \nThis could create chances for a few showers or storms to form along \nthe front as it tracks through, along with increasing humidity.",
